{"authored" [{"question" "q-128452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $(2f(t)-g(t))^{′}$ at $t=-1,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨8\\sqrt{3-t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\ln|2t|⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2}-t,\\,\\pi {t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-128452/review.json" "file_sha256" "2762d68d70498a3a033115afaa82c36756f8a99e2495d4d5f5cad4c634849776" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-128452/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "0a5c8d54f8f1ce2eb26cfcf64f3aef3f2f34d6b735af6fa068da6a25c10e0f47" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-128452/verification.json" "basis" 1411 "rationale" "The original real-valued function uses ln(2t), undefined at the requested t=-1. Its derivative there therefore does not exist. The site accepts its formal derivative <-1,0,-4>. The explicitly authorized local repair replaces ln(2t) by ln|2t|, making that result valid on a neighborhood of -1. Original DOM, screenshot, uncertain solver result and accepted server answer remain preserved. New field and answer identities retain original historical definitions."} {"question" "q-128452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $t=-1$ lies in an open interval where $t<0$ and $3-t>0$, all components are differentiable there. In particular, $\\ln|2t|=\\ln(-2t)$ near $t=-1$, so its derivative is $1/t$.\n\nDifferentiate each vector component:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f'(t)=\\left\\langle-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3-t}},\\pi\\cos(\\pi t),\\frac1t\\right\\rangle,\n\\qquad\n\\mathbf g'(t)=\\langle 2t-1,2\\pi t,-2t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nThe sum and constant multiple rules give\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf f-\\mathbf g)'(t)=2\\mathbf f'(t)-\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nAt $t=-1$,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f'(-1)=\\langle-2,-\\pi,-1\\rangle,\n\\qquad\n\\mathbf g'(-1)=\\langle-3,-2\\pi,2\\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf f-\\mathbf g)'(-1)\n=2\\langle-2,-\\pi,-1\\rangle-\\langle-3,-2\\pi,2\\rangle\n=\\boxed{\\langle-1,0,-4\\rangle}.\n$$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-128452/review.json" "file_sha256" "2762d68d70498a3a033115afaa82c36756f8a99e2495d4d5f5cad4c634849776" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-128452/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "0a5c8d54f8f1ce2eb26cfcf64f3aef3f2f34d6b735af6fa068da6a25c10e0f47" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-128452/verification.json" "basis" 1411 "rationale" "The original real-valued function uses ln(2t), undefined at the requested t=-1. Its derivative there therefore does not exist. The site accepts its formal derivative <-1,0,-4>. The explicitly authorized local repair replaces ln(2t) by ln|2t|, making that result valid on a neighborhood of -1. Original DOM, screenshot, uncertain solver result and accepted server answer remain preserved. New field and answer identities retain original historical definitions."} {"question" "q-128452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,0,-4⟩"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-128452/review.json" "file_sha256" "2762d68d70498a3a033115afaa82c36756f8a99e2495d4d5f5cad4c634849776" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-128452/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "0a5c8d54f8f1ce2eb26cfcf64f3aef3f2f34d6b735af6fa068da6a25c10e0f47" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-128452/verification.json" "basis" 1411 "rationale" "The original real-valued function uses ln(2t), undefined at the requested t=-1. Its derivative there therefore does not exist. The site accepts its formal derivative <-1,0,-4>. The explicitly authorized local repair replaces ln(2t) by ln|2t|, making that result valid on a neighborhood of -1. Original DOM, screenshot, uncertain solver result and accepted server answer remain preserved. New field and answer identities retain original historical definitions."} {"question" "q-128458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $(2f(t)+5g(t))^{′}$ at $t=1,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3+t} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1) \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2t-3 \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ (t+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the sum rule, we have \n \n\n$$\n(2f(t)+5g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)+5{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(2\\sqrt{3+t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3+t}} \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+1)^{2})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 2(t+1)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence , we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(1)+5g(1))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(1)+5{g}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3+1}} \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1-1) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2(1) \\\\ 2(1+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "v