" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4t-7 \\\\ 3t-2 \\\\ 5t-1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}8t-14 \\\\ 6t-5 \\\\ 10t-3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ t \\\\ {t}^{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{3}{{t}^{3}}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}t+\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ {t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{3}+3t\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}2u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=2t+2$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(2u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(3)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2u \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2u(t) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2(2t+2) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(u)={e}^{u+1}\\,i+{e}^{2u}\\,j+\\frac{1}{e}\\,k$ and $u(t)=2{t}^{2}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)=f′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{u+1})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{2u})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\frac{1}{e}\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2u}\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2t}\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})=4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\ (f∘u)^{′}(t) & =({e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+2{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j)4t \\\\  & =4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+6t{e}^{2t}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i-8{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t{e}^{2t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{4t}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{2t}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $g(u)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{u}⟩$ and $u(t)={e}^{2t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}0,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})=2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{u(t)},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}(t)}⟩{u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}⟨\\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{({e}^{2t})^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{{e}^{2t}},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{{e}^{4t}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/1