loper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $g(u)=⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1),\\,1⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u+1},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})=-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(u(t))^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)+1},\\,0⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{t}{1+t},\\,0⟩\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}) \\\\  & =⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,-\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12857