r/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-(\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2477.json" "file_sha256" "01b8d6499d07800eb9b95f8bce49f334319a3950ef97980325140762f936b5f8" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2477.json" "file_sha256" "01b8d6499d07800eb9b95f8bce49f334319a3950ef97980325140762f936b5f8" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)'$ where $[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t) = t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2478.json" "file_sha256" "48bd0d854cfb4f4319ba0bcfc20e901ab2343a3894412ce6ed3bd30967428aa3" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)g(t)+u(t){g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+t\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t+1){e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2478.json" "file_sha256" "48bd0d854cfb4f4319ba0bcfc20e901ab2343a3894412ce6ed3bd30967428aa3" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t),$ if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2479.json" "file_sha256" "765bde555a8bc807f976fac78ce3f31bcead1429fa6f4d87a1da8767a5281b76" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2}+5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(4u)k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})=6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+4\\,k){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{3}}\\,i+2(2{t}^{3})\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot 6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}\\,i+24{t}^{5}\\,j+24{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2479.json" "file_sha256" "765bde555a8bc807f976fac78ce3f31bcead1429fa6f4d87a1da8767a5281b76" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+{t}^{2}j \\\\ g(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}i+{e}^{t}j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2480.json" "file_sha256" "485f507a0ab0ee75c27ca3bacaf1d175187229531f900b14fab6eef945434caf" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}f(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+2t\\,j, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}g(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t)\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\[3pt]\n&= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + e^t \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) +\n\\left(\\sqrt{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + t^2 \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2}  \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j  \\right) \\[3pt]\t\t \n&=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}}  +2te^t    +  \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right)    + t^2e^t \\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2}  -  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t   + t^2e^t  \\[3pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t.\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2480.json" "file_sha256" "485f507a0ab0ee75c27ca3bacaf1d175187229531f900b14fab6eef945434caf" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [] "usage" {"q-128587" [] "q-128458" [] "q-128896" [] "q-33260" [] "q-70685" [] "q-32837" [] "q-32860" [] "q-32498" [] "q-71225" [] "q-71227" [] "e-2480" [] "q-32869" [] "q-32503" [] "q-70681" [] "e-2477" [] "q-128452" [] "e-2478" [] "q-128570" [] "q-71230" [] "q-128586" [] "q-32298" [] "e-2479" [] "q-127998" [] "q-128477" []} "basis" 1411 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186113463 17592186113464 17592186113465 17592186113466 17592186113467 17592186113481 17592186113482 17592186113483 17592186113484 17592186113485 17592186305617 17592186305618 17592186305619 17592186305620 17592186305621 17592186305631 17592186305632 17592186305633 17592186305634 17592186305635 17592186305638 17592186305639 17592186305640 17592186305641 17592186305642 17592186305645 17592186305646 17592186305647 17592186305648 17592186305649 17592186305652 17592186305653 175